     Your best bet is to find someone nearby who has both net access and
a tape drive, and have him or her make you a tape.  The last time it was
posted to comp.sources.games, the distribution was in 56 parts! (each
roughly 100 blocks).  It's not very practical to repost something that big...

     The sources are available via ftp, or via uucp (from just about any
comp.sources.games archive site), or via DECnet on NSI/DECnet (formerly
SPAN).  Sources and binaries for NetHack 3.0j (aka 3.0 patchlevel 10)
are on the DECUS Fall'90 Symposium VAX SIG Collection Tapes in directory
[VAX90B2.RANKIN.GAMES].  Due to a last second update, it ended up as a
compressed saveset rather than getting unpacked into individual files,
and the out-of-date 'readme' file says 3.0 patchlevel 9.

     Here are some network locations where you could find it (these are
all in the U.S.; there are comp.sources.games archive sites in Europe, but
I don't happen to have their addresses):

    site              location        description
----------------    ------------    ---------------
uars.acd.ucar.edu   [.SRC.NETHACK]  sources and VMS binaries, in VMS format
  ACDURS::SYS$LCL:[SRC.NETHACK]     same location, on NSI/DECnet  (9583::)
hamlet.caltech.edu  [.NETHACK]      same as above
  HAMLET::ANON_ROOT:[NETHACK]       ditto  (5970::)
linc.cis.upenn.edu  pub/NH3.0       sources spread across many uuencoded,
                                    compressed, tar files; also, binaries for
                                    several microcomputers in subdirectories.
ftp.uu.net          comp.sources.games/volume7/NetHack3     shar files for
                                    3.0 and also patches 1 through 10.
                    comp.sources.games/volume10/nethack3p9  shar files for
                                    3.0pl9; get patch 10 from ../volume7
gatekeeper.dec.com  pub/comp.sources.games/volume10/nethack3p9  (see uunet)
                    pub/comp.sources.games/volume12/NetHack3    patch 10

The first two sites (acdurs and hamlet) have VMS specific packaging and
contain both a source package and a binaries package (each about 3500 blocks).
linc has the 'master' copy, but packaged in Unix format; bug reports should
go to "nethack-bugs@linc.cis.upenn.edu".  uunet and gatekeeper are two
comp.sources.games archive sites; they both have lots of old versions
laying around--be sure to get the latest, which is 3.0pl10.

